/P 222 0 R
/T (I was born in New York but when I was a young kid my family moved to Los Angeles. While living in LA for as long as I can remember, my dad has always made an effort to try to get me to go to Israel, but I would always think, what about working or college and really taking that first big leap into adulthood. So when the conversation of Yeshivah came up with my dad I was super conflicted because obviously I want to learn and grow a connection with Hashem, but at the same time I can get a head start on adulthood and become financially responsible. )
/E (I was born in New York but when I was a young kid my family moved to Los Angeles. While living in LA for as long as I can remember, my dad has always made an effort to try to get me to go to Israel, but I would always think, what about working or college and really taking that first big leap into adulthood. So when the conversation of Yeshivah came up with my dad I was super conflicted because obviously I want to learn and grow a connection with Hashem, but at the same time I can get a head start on adulthood and become financially responsible. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
