2060 0 obj
<<
/Title (I was born in New York but when I was a young kid my family moved to Los Angeles. While living in LA for as long as I can remember, my dad has always made an effort to try to get me to go to Israel, but I would always think, what about working or college and really taking that first big leap into adulthood. So when the conversation of Yeshivah came up with my dad I was super conflicted because obviously I want to learn and grow a connection with Hashem, but at the same time I can get a head start on adulthood and become financially responsible.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2043 0 R
/Prev 2053 0 R
/Next 2061 0 R
>>
endobj
2061 0 obj
<<
/Title (After a few more discussions I decided that I would go to Yeshivat Moreshet Yerushalayim. When I made the decision to come I was extremely nervous. I was nervous that being on my own would result in me leaving the year early. Also, not knowing so many kids was a super nerve-racking feeling.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2043 0 R
/Prev 2060 0 R
/Next 2054 0 R
>>
endobj
